 from 277,248 NAND gates"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://somethingbig.ai/computer"}},"_tags":["story","author_rossant","story_49871018","front_page"],"author":"rossant","children":[49871337,49897616,49897656,49898498,49898677,49898804,49899430,49899778,49900863,49901045,49901293,49901849,49902047,49902463,49902654],"created_at":"2026-09-27T21:26:06Z","created_at_i":1790544366,"num_comments":68,"objectID":"49871018","points":122,"story_id":49871018,"title":"NAND-16: a computer built from 277,248 NAND gates","updated_at":"2026-09-30T06:06:40Z","url":"https://somethingbig.ai/computer"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"bketelsen"},"story_text":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"One of the things that Windows really got right is WSL2. I drive an atomic Linux distro for daily use, but wanted a way to develop with multiple different distros with that same WSL UX.  NSL is my answer. It is a faithful reproduction of the developer experience, powered by a single VM that hosts one or more systemd-nspawn containers with your development instances. Host file edits and port sharing come along for the ride, just like WSL. Take a look and tell me what you think... It's yet another step in my long journey to keep my host installation free from all the changing and breaking dev dependencies that force a reinstall every few months."},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Show HN: NSL \u2013 WSL for Linux"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://frostyard.github.io/nsl/"}},"_tags":["story","author_bketelsen","story_49894351","show_hn","front_page"],"author":"bketelsen","children":[49895906,49895908,49895912,49896006,49896021,49896117,49896132,49896459,49896511,49896813,49897371,49897495,49897684,49898211,49898237,49898241,49898327,49900759,49901953,49902905,49903067,49903210,49903850,49904242,49904278,49904738,49905003],"created_at":"2026-09-29T14:51:36Z","created_at_i":1790693496,"num_comments":77,"objectID":"49894351","points":112,"story_id":49894351,"story_text":"One of the things that Windows really got right is WSL2. I drive an atomic Linux distro for daily use, but wanted a way to develop with multiple different distros with that same WSL UX.  NSL is my answer. It is a faithful reproduction of the developer experience, powered by a single VM that hosts one or more systemd-nspawn containers with your development instances. Host file edits and port sharing come along for the ride, just like WSL. Take a look and tell me what you think... It&#x27;s yet another step in my long journey to keep my host installation free from all the changing and breaking dev dependencies that force a reinstall every few months.","title":"Show HN: NSL \u2013 WSL for Linux","updated_at":"2026-09-30T06:09:40Z","url":"https://frostyard.github.io/nsl/"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"ilamont"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"NASA asked several former SR-71A staffers to help secret restart"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://aviationweek.com/defense/aircraft-propulsion/nasa-asked-several-former-sr-71a-staffers-help-secret-restart"}},"_tags":["story","author_ilamont","story_49890733","front_page"],"author":"ilamont","children":[49892010,49902562,49902624,49902679,49902690,49902714,49902729,49902739,49902784,49902825,49902895,49902940,49902955,49902963,49903114,49903154,49903252,49903271,49903284,49903305,49903786,49904129,49904809,49904847],"created_at":"2026-09-29T10:10:20Z","created_at_i":1790676620,"num_comments":102,"objectID":"49890733","points":111,"story_id":49890733,"title":"NASA asked several former SR-71A staffers to help secret restart","updated_at":"2026-09-30T06:11:55Z","url":"https://aviationweek.com/defense/aircraft-propulsion/nasa-asked-several-former-sr-71a-staffers-help-secret-restart"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLeve